-- title:
--   Diamond ⟨ d⟩ preserves components and crossings mod p
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $5\le M$ and $p\nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a $p$-th cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, with $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, containing $p$ in its maximal ideal and some preimage of $\zeta$, acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$, and let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent image the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ and an $A$-algebra, and let $X_s$ denote the fibre `pullback (ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j) (specMap A k)` of the two-chart model over $\operatorname{Spec} k$. Given proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$, geometrically integral curves $c_1\colon C_1\to\operatorname{Spec} k$, $c_2\colon C_2\to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and closed immersions $i_1,i_2$ of them into $X_s$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$, assume every point of $X_s$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, that `pullback i₁ i₂` is reduced, and that its point set has cardinality $n$ with $0<n$. Assume further: a section $\varepsilon$ of [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, sections $\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2$ of $c_1,c_2$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ with $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ equal to the base change `sectionBaseChange k ε`; an integer $d$ coprime to $Mp$ with $d\equiv 1 \pmod M$; an $L$-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of $K$ agreeing, under the identification of $K$ with [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, with [`ModularCurve.baseChangeAut L (ModularCurve.diamondAut (M * p) d)`](def/ModularCurve_X1Diamond.html#L24); an automorphism $w$ of [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) over $\operatorname{Spec} A$; and a ring endomorphism $\rho$ of the finite chart algebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135) (the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$) inducing $\theta$ on elements, such that $\operatorname{Spec}\rho$ followed by the chart morphism [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231) equals that chart morphism followed by $w$. Writing $w_s =$ `curveChange w.hom hw (specMap A k)` for the induced automorphism of $X_s$, the conclusion is threefold: there is an automorphism $\alpha_1$ of $C_1$ over $k$ with $i_1\circ\alpha_1 = w_s\circ i_1$; there is an automorphism $\alpha_2$ of $C_2$ over $k$ with $i_2\circ\alpha_2 = w_s\circ i_2$; and for every $k$-point $z$ of `pullback i₁ i₂`, the image of $z$ under the first projection followed by $i_1$ is unchanged by $w_s$.
--
--   This is the geometric statement that a diamond automorphism $\langle d\rangle$ with $d\equiv 1 \pmod M$ acts on the special fibre at $p$ of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ by preserving each of the two covering components and fixing each crossing point. It is the input used in deducing that such diamond operators act trivially on the toric part attached to the special fibre, via [`ModularCurve.XOneP.comp_heckeHom_diamondGen_eq_of_comp_torus_specialFibre_of_representsRelSubPic_abelJacobi_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.comp_heckeHom_diamondGen_eq_of_comp_torus_specialFibre_of_representsRelSubPic_abelJacobi_twoChartModel_x1_mul).
